A||||1||CD||Auto Transmission or Electrical problem in an 87 GT||||1||
Z||000000||CD||07-15-2000||04:36 PM||||I recently replaced a broken EGR tube and EGR valve as a result of a high idle and a code 35.  I started the car and it purred like a kitten.  The car hasn’t idled that good since I bought it.  Anyway, I hop in the car anxious for a test spin and every time I shift into a drive gear (Reverse, Drive, First, Second) the car immediately quits.  The car doesn’t sputter and die, it just quits, almost electrical like.  Has anyone had this symptom before?  Should I replace the IAC?  Could it be the neutral/park switch or something else electrical?  Any thoughts on the throttle linkage or TV cable?||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||07-15-2000||04:53 PM||||Sounds like your torque converter clutch is locked up. Try unplugging it. It is a connector on the firewall side of the trans next to the exhaust. It has 4 pins. Then try putting it in gear.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||3
